  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic autonomy and food security via agroecology to promote youth and women of the indigenous community of Nahuizalco, Sonsonate, El Salvador</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fundacin para el Desarrollo Socioeconmico y Restauracin Ambiental (FUNDESYRAM) will engage Nhuatl Pipil residents from four communities in Nahuizalco department of Sonsonate to increase incomes and improve living conditions by organizing farmers and introducing agroecological practices vegetable gardens and small animal production. It will also train farmers in marketing skills and develop marketplaces to sell their production. Some 720 individuals mainly indigenous women and youths will benefit directly and 2000 more indirectly.</narrative>
  </description>
